      "global_exposure": "All semantic components have nonzero dense full-scene samples; numerical exposure is diagnostic only. Final ordinary views and exact-subject details independently determine readability.",
      "scientific_caveats": "Actual ROM61125 and USNM57700 specimen pixels independently inspected; short anterior shield, long limbless ringed abdomen and paired broad caudal paddles supported. Museum morphology specifies approximately ten antennal segments each bearing a ventral spine, 2-4 front leg pairs and 13 abdomen rings. Three modeled leg pairs are a disclosed choice, not fossil certainty. Fine head/limb anatomy is weakly known and full1974 monograph was not obtained/read. Perspicaris comparative specimen shows much larger enclosing valve region and narrow forked tail. Final Plenocaris is structurally distinct, but topological subdivision alone does not depict segmented antennae. This is a frozen visible-feature failure, not a new hard dimensional gate.",
      "repairs": [
